<title>USA: Fannie Mae to redeem 2 notes, 1 debenture.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae to redeem 2 notes, 1 debenture.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal National Mortgage Association (Fannie Mae) said Friday it will redeem all outstanding amounts of two medium-term notes totaling $150 million and one debenture issue totaling $500 million.</p>
<p>The issues will be redeemed on the following dates, at a price equal to 100 percent of the principal amount plus accrued interest.</p>
<p>MEDIUM-TERM NOTES</p>
<p> Principal     Interest    Maturity		     Redemption</p>
<p> Amount	    Rate	 Date	     Cusip	    Date</p>
<p> $100,000,000   6.62%    July 24, 1998    31364CGE2    July 24</p>
<p> $50,000,000    6.83%    July 5, 2000     31364BEZ9    Aug 22</p>
<p>DEBENTURE</p>
<p> Principal     Interest Maturity			  Redemption</p>
<p> Amount	  Rate     Date	   Series    Cusip	Date</p>
<p>$500,000,000   7.00%   Aug 11, 1999 SM-1999-J 31359CAV7 Aug 11</p>
